\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Theorem}
\title{Converging coefficients share the block field}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{Keep the coefficients, the mass, and the limiting
second-order coefficient #{\kappa} of \ref{fdip-00G0}, and
set #{m^2=\frac{\mu}{\kappa}}. Let #{\varphi} be the rescaled field
of that statement, for #{N=BM} with integers #{B\ge 1} and
#{M\ge 1}, and with #{N} large enough that #{Q_N} is a
positive precision parameter. Write #{A_b} for the mean of
the #{M} consecutive coordinates of #{\varphi} on the
half-open interval from #{b/B} to #{(b+1)/B}. As
#{M\to\infty}, the covariance operator of
#{(A_0,\ldots,A_{B-1})} on the counting space of these
#{B} block labels converges to the covariance operator of
\ref{fdip-00BO} at mass squared #{m^2}. Its canonical kernel
is #{C(b,c)=\mathbb E(A_bA_c)}. Let #{F}
be a Hölder version, of this mass #{m}, from
\ref{fdip-00BE}. The joint law of the block means converges
to the joint law of the integral means of #{F} over the
#{B} equal arcs. Those integral means determine the
\vocabk{dyadic increment}{fdip-00E5} of #{F}.}

\proof{
\p{Declare the counting basis of site indicators. The spectral
expansion in the proof of \ref{fdip-00G0}
gives the kernel of the counting covariance operator,
##{\mathbb E\bigl(\varphi(u)\varphi(v)\bigr)
=\kappa\sum_{p=0}^{N-1}\lambda_p^{-1}
\exp\bigl(2\pi i p(u-v)/N\bigr),}
with #{\lambda_p=\mu_N+N^2\alpha_N(2\pi p/N)}. The block
mean #{A_b} averages #{M} consecutive sites. The sum over
one block is geometric. For the zero mode it contributes
#{M}, and for every other mode its squared modulus, divided
by #{M^2}, equals
##{\frac{B^2\sin^2(\pi p/B)}{N^2\sin^2(\pi p/N)},}
because #{|1-e^{i\phi}|^2=4\sin^2\frac{\phi}{2}} and #{M=N/B}.
Hence
##{\mathbb E(A_bA_c)
=\sum_{p=0}^{N-1}t_{N,p}
\exp\bigl(2\pi i p(b-c)/B\bigr),}
where #{t_{N,0}=\frac{\kappa}{\mu_N}} and, for the other modes,
##{t_{N,p}
=\frac{\kappa B^2\sin^2(\pi p/B)}
{N^2\sin^2(\pi p/N)\,\lambda_p}.}}

\p{Take the representative of #{p} in a symmetric range of
length #{N}. The chord bound in the proof of
\ref{fdip-00BO} gives #{\sin(\pi |p|/N)\ge 2|p|/N} for
#{1\le |p|\le N/2}, so #{N^2\sin^2(\pi p/N)\ge 4p^2}. For
every sufficiently large #{N} one has #{\mu_N\ge\frac{\mu}{2}}, and
#{\lambda_p\ge\mu_N}, while the squared sine in the
numerator is at most #{1}. Thus
#{t_{N,p}\le\kappa B^2/(2\mu p^2)}. Extend #{t_{N,p}} by
#{0} outside that range. The comparison is summable over
the nonzero integers. For each fixed #{p\ne 0}, the symbol
limit in \ref{fdip-00G0} and
#{N\sin(\pi p/N)\to\pi p} give
numerator #{\kappa B^2\sin^2(\pi p/B)} and denominator
#{(\pi p)^2(\mu+4\pi^2\kappa p^2)}. Dividing both by
#{\kappa} cancels the leading factor and replaces
#{\mu+4\pi^2\kappa p^2} by #{m^2+(2\pi p)^2}, so
##{t_{N,p}\to
\frac{B^2\sin^2(\pi p/B)}
{(\pi p)^2\bigl(m^2+(2\pi p)^2\bigr)}.}
The constant mode tends to #{1/m^2}. Split the series into
#{|p|\le P} and the tail. The tail is smaller than any
prescribed positive tolerance, uniformly in all sufficiently
large #{N}, once #{P} is large. Each of the finitely many
remaining terms converges. The resulting kernel is the
canonical kernel of the covariance operator of
\ref{fdip-00BO} at mass squared #{m^2}.}

\p{\ref{fdip-00BP} identifies that kernel with the
covariance of the means #{B\int_I F} for a field with the
covariance #{G} of \ref{fdip-00BG}. From that
identification, the argument of \ref{fdip-00ED} shows that
these integral means determine the dyadic increment of
#{F}. The block means are centered Gaussian, as linear
images of #{x}. The integral means are centered Gaussian,
singular covariance included, by the same argument. Both
laws are fixed by their covariances, so the block-mean laws
converge to the laws of the integral means.}
}
